Role: Product Owner – Communication Channels &amp; AI
Location: Manchester
Hours: Monday-Friday 8:45am-5:15pm
Package: £80k OTE 
&nbsp;
As Product Owner - Technical Products, your role is to own and continuously improve PHMG's Technical product portfolio, ensuring Cloud Telephony, AI Receptionist and CCE deliver measurable client value, operational&nbsp;quality&nbsp;and long-term commercial growth.&nbsp;
You are accountable for translating client needs, technology capability, partner opportunities and commercial priorities into scalable products and service models that strengthen adoption,&nbsp;retention&nbsp;and PHMG's competitive position.&nbsp;
Through H2 2026, you will lead the evolution of the&nbsp;technical&nbsp;product portfolio by bringing together product performance, platform capability, roadmap execution, client outcomes, commercial discipline, operational&nbsp;readiness&nbsp;and cross-functional alignment into one coherent product improvement agenda.&nbsp;
&nbsp;
Key Objectives&nbsp;
Core Accountability&nbsp;

Own the strategy, design and ongoing performance of Cloud Telephony, AI&nbsp;Receptionist&nbsp;and CCE.
Set a clear,&nbsp;prioritised&nbsp;roadmap that balances client value, technical feasibility, commercial return, operational&nbsp;capacity&nbsp;and partner dependency.
Ensure Technical products are positioned, sold,&nbsp;onboarded,&nbsp;serviced&nbsp;and renewed in a way that delivers measurable value for clients.
Define the product standards, service&nbsp;models&nbsp;and client journeys that CS and Technical Production can execute consistently.
Bring clarity to build,&nbsp;buy&nbsp;and partner decisions so product direction is deliberate, commercially&nbsp;disciplined&nbsp;and scalable.

&nbsp;
Technical Product Strategy &amp; Roadmap&nbsp;

Define the long-term direction for Cloud Telephony, AI Receptionist and CCE, including the sequence of capability,&nbsp;integrations&nbsp;and service-model changes.
Prioritise&nbsp;AI Receptionist growth across both horizontal capability and the vertical use cases where PHMG has the strongest right to win.
Create a clear approach for CCE in the existing base, reducing&nbsp;under-utilisation&nbsp;and turning technical&nbsp;review, onboarding and value evidence into retention levers.
Partner with the Creative Product&nbsp;Owner&nbsp;so the full product set feels coherent to clients and to the teams selling and servicing it.

&nbsp;
&nbsp;
Client Experience, Adoption &amp; Value Evidence&nbsp;

Define the client experience for&nbsp;Technical&nbsp;products across onboarding, configuration, in-life usage,&nbsp;renewal&nbsp;and offboarding.
Clarify how&nbsp;clients&nbsp;access, configure and understand product value through the portal, including call flows, AI Receptionist&nbsp;behaviour, CCE setup and usage analytics.
Ensure CS has the standards, data and language needed to&nbsp;evidence&nbsp;value, drive&nbsp;adoption&nbsp;and manage client expectations confidently.
Identify&nbsp;where clients slow, stall or disengage, and build product or service-model interventions that protect retention.

&nbsp;
Commercial Performance &amp; Partner Discipline&nbsp;

Own the commercial logic of the&nbsp;Technical&nbsp;portfolio, including pricing, CAC, cost-to-serve, gross margin, revenue&nbsp;performance&nbsp;and investment cases.
Operationalise&nbsp;the&nbsp;GoTo&nbsp;resell model with clear pricing, service,&nbsp;process&nbsp;and margin controls while protecting the partner relationship.
Use data to assess where&nbsp;Technical&nbsp;products create incremental value, where they&nbsp;cannibalise&nbsp;existing activity and where the model needs to change.
Make active trade-offs between speed, quality, margin, client&nbsp;experience&nbsp;and platform investment.

&nbsp;
Operational Delivery &amp; Launch Readiness&nbsp;

Work with Technical Production and Tech to define standards, SLAs, runbooks and support models for each product and release.
Ensure new capabilities do not go live until operational&nbsp;readiness,&nbsp;client communications, CS&nbsp;briefings&nbsp;and support routes are clear.
Create tight governance for launch decisions, technical dependencies, client escalations, recurring provisioning&nbsp;issues&nbsp;and partner constraints.
Keep accountability clear between Product,&nbsp;Tech&nbsp;and Product&nbsp;Operations&nbsp;so issues are solved at the right level rather than absorbed by CS.

&nbsp;
Insight, Reporting &amp; Continuous Improvement&nbsp;

Maintain a reliable view of product performance across adoption, usage, NPS, retention, revenue, margin, service&nbsp;issues&nbsp;and operational friction.
Build structured feedback loops with CS, Client Insights, Sales,&nbsp;Tech&nbsp;and Technical Production to&nbsp;identify&nbsp;product problems worth solving.
Turn recurring client or operational issues into permanent product, process,&nbsp;reporting&nbsp;or service-model improvements.
Use performance data to make early decisions before product issues become retention,&nbsp;margin&nbsp;or client-experience risks.

